.TH HEARTBEAT_MONITOR.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
heartbeat_monitor.py \- UDP heartbeat liveness monitor with web dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B heartbeat_monitor.py
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR dark | light ]
.RB [ \-d | \-\-daemon ]
.RB [ \-\-pid\-file
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-file
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B heartbeat_monitor.py
listens for JSON heartbeat datagrams on a UDP port (IPv4 and IPv6), keeps
the most recent heartbeat for each sender
.IR name ,
and serves a dashboard, a JSON API and a Server\-Sent Events stream over HTTP.
A sender is shown healthy while the time since its last heartbeat, measured
on the monitor's clock, is at most its timeout; otherwise it is shown timed out.
A sender silent for longer than
.B monitor.cleanup_after
seconds is removed from the display entirely.
.PP
Each address family has its own listener thread.
The IPv6 socket is bound with
.B IPV6_V6ONLY
so it can share the port number with the IPv4 socket.
The web server is Flask's built\-in threaded server.
.PP
In the control room the program is started by
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
which runs it in daemon mode on HTTP port 8081 and UDP port 9999.
.PP
The datagram format and HTTP routes are specified in
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
YAML configuration file.
Default
.IR config.yaml .
A relative name that does not exist in the current directory is searched
for in
.IR ~/.config/heartbeat_monitor/ ,
.IR /etc/heartbeat_monitor/ ,
the
.I config/
directory next to the script, and the script's own directory.
If it is found nowhere, a warning is logged and built\-in defaults are used.
No file named
.I config.yaml
ships with the package; the shipped file is
.IR config/heartbeat_config.yaml ,
so pass it explicitly.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Run Flask in debug mode.
This exposes the Werkzeug interactive debugger on
.BR server.web_host ,
which is 0.0.0.0 by default.
Do not use on a networked DAQ host.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fIdark\fR | \fIlight\fR
Default dashboard theme; overrides
.BR monitor.theme .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Detach with a double fork, change to
.BR daemon.working_dir ,
redirect stdout and stderr to the log file, and write the PID file.
Also enabled by
.B daemon.enabled: true
in the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " path"
PID file in daemon mode.
Default:
.B daemon.pid_file
or
.IR /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.pid .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Log file in daemon mode.
Default:
.B daemon.log_file
or
.IR /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.log .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/heartbeat_config.yaml
Shipped configuration; see
.BR heartbeat_config.yaml (5).
.TP
.I /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.pid
Default PID file in daemon mode.
The start script uses
.I heartbeat_monitor.pid
in the checkout instead.
.TP
.I /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.log
Default log file in daemon mode.
.PP
In daemon mode the process sets its umask to 0, so the PID and log files are
created with mode 0666.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
Overrides
.BR server.web_port .
Must be an integer; any other non\-empty value aborts startup with a Python
.BR ValueError .
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
Overrides both
.B server.udp_port
and
.BR server.udp6_port .
Same parsing as above.
.PP
Precedence for ports:
.B CRS_PORT_*
environment, then the configuration file, then the built\-in defaults
(HTTP 8080, UDP 9999).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, or the parent process after a successful fork in daemon mode.
.TP
.B 1
Uncaught exception during startup, for example the HTTP port already in use
or an invalid
.B CRS_PORT_*
value.
.PP
A failure to bind a UDP port does not cause a non\-zero exit: it ends only
that listener thread, and the HTTP server keeps running.
.SH EXAMPLES
Foreground, with the shipped configuration and the control\-room ports:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
CRS_PORT_HTTP=8081 venv/bin/python heartbeat_monitor.py \e
    \-c config/heartbeat_config.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query the state:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
curl \-s localhost:8081/api/health
curl \-s localhost:8081/api/systems | python3 \-m json.tool
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1),
.BR heartbeat_sender (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
.BR heartbeat_config.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7)
